[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: ZEF TESTS — verification work items
UID: ZEF-TEST-DOC
VERSION: 1.0.0
DATE: 2026-10-11
PREFIX: ZEF-TEST
ROOT: False
OPTIONS:
  ENABLE_MID: False
  MARKUP: Text

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
TEST items identify executable verification scenarios. Each item names the
behavior under test, traces to the applicable WHAT or INTERFACE record, and
points to the source test that implements the scenario. The current suite is a
host C11 suite using the public ``zef.h`` header and the linked ``zef`` library.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Public surface and Message ownership

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-TEST-001
TITLE: Public configuration and consumer compilation
STATEMENT: >>>
Compile a consumer translation unit against the public header and
exercise the published configuration types, constants, complete runtime
structures, result values, action values, and callback signatures. Compile-time
assertions check the default limits and tick width, while zero-initialized
instances cover every complete caller-owned runtime structure.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-004
- TYPE: File
  FORMAT: Sourcecode
  PATH: tests/zef_test_work.c

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-TEST-002
TITLE: Fixed-pool Message construction and typed access
STATEMENT: >>>
Initialize caller-owned pools, construct a typed dynamic Message,
verify smallest-suitable-pool selection, read its topic and payload size, and
obtain the typed payload after transfer and dequeue. The scenario then requests
a payload that fits only the larger pool and verifies that the larger pool is
selected and reclaimed after release, while the mutable typed accessor is
checked during construction.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-010
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-012
- TYPE: File
  FORMAT: Sourcecode
  PATH: tests/zef_test_work.c

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-TEST-003
TITLE: Dynamic claims, static Messages, and deferred ownership
STATEMENT: >>>
Exercise retain and release, final pool reclamation, static Message
no-op cleanup, and ``postpone`` reference sharing without copying the Message
storage. The dynamic scenario retains, releases, postpones, and takes the same
Message while checking reference sharing and final pool availability; the static
scenario performs generic retain/release cleanup without changing lifetime.
<<<
