  VALUE: ZEF-WHAT-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-WHAT-012
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-011
- TYPE: File
  FORMAT: Sourcecode
  PATH: tests/zef_test_work.c

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-TEST-004
TITLE: Panic boundary and failure-state preservation
STATEMENT: >>>
Catch the application panic callback for pool exhaustion, Mailbox overflow,
invalid pool, Mailbox, and static-Message arguments, invalid mutable lifecycle
access, checked-payload size mismatch, and release of a reclaimed Message.
Verify each reported panic reason and confirm that a failed allocation leaves
pool statistics unchanged and a full-Mailbox post leaves its sender pointer
intact before completing the valid cleanup path.
<<<
