[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Mailboxes and Machines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-TEST-010
TITLE: Mailbox ordering, statistics, and selective removal
STATEMENT: >>>
Exercise FIFO delivery, front insertion ordering, occupancy and
minimum-free-space observations, empty take behavior, and stable predicate
removal while preserving the remaining static Message order. A second
capacity-two Mailbox also exercises front insertion on an empty ring and
normal posts and takes after the monotonic indices wrap. A dynamic removal
case verifies that removed claims are released while the retained entry stays
available, and the public capacity statistic is checked.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-WHAT-031
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-013
- TYPE: File
  FORMAT: Sourcecode
  PATH: tests/zef_test_work.c

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-TEST-011
TITLE: Hierarchical Machine startup and transitions
STATEMENT: >>>
Start a descriptor graph with an initial child, dispatch a Message
that transitions between sibling states, verify leave and enter order, repeat
the operation as a self-transition, and verify parent-handler bubbling from
the child state. An outside transition target is rejected without changing the
current state. The public current-state result is checked after each path.
<<<
