[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-TEST-012
TITLE: Nested Machine common-ancestor transitions
STATEMENT: >>>
Construct a hierarchy with a root, two nested application branches, sibling
leaves, and a separate emergency branch, each with initial-child links. Start
at the deepest initial leaf, then transition between siblings, across nested
branches, to an ancestor that re-enters its initial chain, across the root,
and through a self-transition. Compare the complete hook-event sequence after
each dispatch to verify reverse source exits, the lowest common ancestor, target
entry order, initial-child descent, and parent-handler bubbling; reject an
outside target without changing the current state.
<<<
