[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Reactors, Kernel, and topics

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-TEST-020
TITLE: Reactor lifecycle and cooperative priority scheduling
STATEMENT: >>>
Register multiple Reactors at explicit identities, including a temporary gap,
and start them out of identity order. Post work to their Mailboxes and verify
highest-identity selection, strict dispatch priority, and the no-work result
after delivery. One Reactor receives queued work before it starts to verify
that it is ignored until startup.
The no-work path also enters ``run_forever`` with an idle callback that exits
the fixture, verifying that idle is called instead of dispatching stale work.
<<<
