- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-WHAT-070
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEF-IF-040
- TYPE: File
  FORMAT: Sourcecode
  PATH: tests/zef_test_work.c

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-TEST-033
TITLE: Timer ownership and same-tick ordering corners
STATEMENT: >>>
Arm two topic Timers for the same tick and verify their queued order matches
arm order without invoking a handler during Clock advancement. Then initialize
a payload-based periodic Timer, stop it with a pending delivery, take and
release that delivery, verify the Timer retains its base claim, and re-arm it
successfully before terminal cancellation. A second dynamic Timer is cancelled
with a pending delivery to verify private-message removal, claim cleanup, and
the ``Z_NOT_RUNNING`` result after cancellation. The same
fixture also checks the configured span overflow panic and the double-arm
lifecycle panic before stopping the valid Timer.
<<<
